WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.160
Since our last update, we’ve made great
progress in the Regeneration areas.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.920
At the end of November, the much anticipated
Kaiapoi Dog Park opened its gates to the public.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.400
The ribbon was cut by Mayor Dan Gordon and
former resident Barbara Townsend, who lived

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.180
on the land where the park is located.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:30.080
Dozens of four-legged locals joined the celebration,
with prizes awarded to Mr Kaiapoi, Miss Kaiapoi,

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.900
best dressed, scruffiest and waggiest tail.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.320
Following a short delay due to the lockdown,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.640
the roading in the surrounding area
has now been upgraded.

00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:44.060
Charles Street now incorporates
what used to be Jollie Street.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.420
It has been resurfaced, and includes a 
new footpath and parking.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:55.280
Over at Norman Kirk Park, the Cass Street
car park is also quickly taking shape.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.559
During the last couple of months, the grass for the sports grounds has established well.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.600
Irrigation has been installed and work on
the softball diamonds is now underway.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.440
Construction is also about to start on the
changing rooms and public toilets.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.220
They are due to be complete in October 
and all going well,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.600
we’ll see the sports fields in use
over the coming summer.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:24.560
On the Kaiapoi River, a second round
of dredging is underway.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.460
After removing the remaining high points by the
Williams Street Bridge, the barge will

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:33.960
move downriver to deal with silt build up
and further improve navigability for vessels.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.940
The walkway between the
Williams Street Bridge and Trousellot park

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.520
is also receiving final repairs.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.000
Once complete, the popular
“teeming” sculpture will return

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.740
following its removal after the earthquakes.

